From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:49:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmgr: show a consumer-switched
 state's real power state

A consumer-switched power state is powered off and on by its consumer
(apple_pmgr_ps_consumer_off() and _on()), which writes the hardware state
directly. genpd keeps its own status, so pm_genpd_summary still reads "on"
for such a state while its consumer has powered it down. On the J604 the
two external display coprocessors power their six states down about five
seconds after boot with nothing attached ("idle: nothing attached:
external display coprocessor and domains down"), and the summary still
lists dispext0/1 cpu, fe and sys as on. Idle power accounting that reads
the summary counts them as held.

Add a read-only consumer_state attribute (on, off or failed) to the
device of each consumer-switched state, read under the lock the switch
takes. Other states do not get the attribute. Nothing else changes.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
index 8ebc62779b..6bcaa4cd1c 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
@@ -1290,10 +1290,49 @@ static const struct dev_pm_ops apple_pmgr_ps_pm_ops = {
 	NOIRQ_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(apple_pmgr_ps_suspend_noirq, apple_pmgr_ps_resume_noirq)
 };
 
+/*
+ * consumer_state (read-only, consumer-switched states only): whether the
+ * consumer has powered the state off. genpd's own status stays "on" for
+ * these states, because the consumer switches the hardware state directly
+ * (apple_pmgr_ps_consumer_off()), so this is where the real state shows.
+ */
+static ssize_t consumer_state_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+				   char *buf)
+{
+	struct apple_pmgr_ps *ps = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	unsigned long flags;
+	const char *state;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&ps->genpd.slock, flags);
+	state = ps->consumer_failed ? "failed" : ps->consumer_off ? "off" : "on";
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ps->genpd.slock, flags);
+	return sysfs_emit(buf, "%s\n", state);
+}
+static DEVICE_ATTR_RO(consumer_state);
+
+static struct attribute *apple_pmgr_ps_attrs[] = {
+	&dev_attr_consumer_state.attr,
+	NULL
+};
+
+static umode_t apple_pmgr_ps_attr_visible(struct kobject *kobj, struct attribute *attr, int n)
+{
+	struct apple_pmgr_ps *ps = dev_get_drvdata(kobj_to_dev(kobj));
+
+	return ps && ps->consumer_switched ? attr->mode : 0;
+}
+
+static const struct attribute_group apple_pmgr_ps_group = {
+	.attrs = apple_pmgr_ps_attrs,
+	.is_visible = apple_pmgr_ps_attr_visible,
+};
+__ATTRIBUTE_GROUPS(apple_pmgr_ps);
+
 static struct platform_driver apple_pmgr_ps_driver = {
 	.probe = apple_pmgr_ps_probe,
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "apple-pmgr-pwrstate",
+		.dev_groups = apple_pmgr_ps_groups,
 		.of_match_table = apple_pmgr_ps_of_match,
 		.pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&apple_pmgr_ps_pm_ops),
 	},
-- 
